summary:
I've heard this a lot. As someone who helped build a company with thousands of remote workers (including the exec team), it's unfortunate to see the pendulum swinging in a way that is definitely hostile to remote hiring. I don't think I could trust remote interviews right now.
Quoting @0xFFA4
@mitchellh It's unfortunate, for me as someone who lives in Africa. Working fully remotely for international companies opened a lot of doors . Opportunities I would not have gotten otherwise. With in-person interviews and in-office this has impacted me massively.

Thank you! Been hearing this a lot more recently by intrepid early adopters who are helping test libghostty. I really believe the reach and adoption and impact of libghostty is going to make Ghostty the app look like the glorified tech demo of libghostty that it kind of is. 😎
Quoting @wiedymi
@mitchellh 's ghostty codebase is amazing, it took me less then a day to build libghostty from source and integrate it in my little macos app

This was meant as a joke but this is actually a serious point highlighting the nuance involved in all of this. Using a Ralph loop for a PoC to move quickly is PERFECT tradeoff of time/money. A+. Shipping that unquestionably to a production, customer-impacting environment? Oof.
Quoting @shan3v
@mitchellh The engineer trying to impress you with their Ralph Wiggum loop ain't gonna make it
